"answer": "According to the provided sources, treatments for rashes may include moisturizers, lotions, baths, cortisone creams to relieve swelling, and antihistamines to relieve itching [MLP-208]. Additionally, for itching associated with rashes, treatments can involve cold compresses, moisturizing lotions, lukewarm or oatmeal baths, and over-the-counter hydrocortisone cream or antihistamines [MLP-3067]. For eczema, a type of rash, treatments may include medicines, skin creams, light therapy, and good skin care [MLP-1215]."
}
